cards[5]{id,category,difficulty,front,back,source,tags}:
  card_001,research,hard,"A Stanford AI is demonstrating the ability to predict future disease risk from a single night of sleep. What physiological signals are being analyzed by this AI?","Physiological signals, such as heart rate variability and breathing patterns, are being analyzed to identify potential health warnings.",ScienceDaily Health,AI;sleep;predictive modeling
  card_002,news,medium,"Who received the 2026 SPIE Harrison H. Barrett Award for their contributions to medical imaging? What is their primary area of research?","Norbert Pelc received the award for developing innovative imaging techniques for studying tumors and immune responses, potentially leading to new cancer therapies.",Stanford Medicine,award;medical imaging;cancer research
  card_003,news,medium,"Envision Radiology recently acquired a private equity-backed imaging center operator named what? What is the potential impact of this acquisition?","Envision Radiology acquired Rezolut. This acquisition may impact referral patterns and access to care in the acquired regions.",Google News Radiology,mergers;imaging networks;access to care
  card_004,research,medium,"A study highlighted the importance of what two factors in preventing the spread of influenza?","Limiting coughing and maintaining well-mixed indoor air were shown to significantly prevent influenza transmission.",ScienceDaily Health,influenza;transmission;ventilation
  card_005,research,hard,"What is the '4x rule' study investigating? What is the significance of the findings?","The '4x rule' study investigates DNA instability. The findings reveal that many individuals have DNA sequences that expand at varying rates, with some experiencing a fourfold increase, potentially linking these expansions to certain diseases.",ScienceDaily Health,genetics;DNA instability;disease risk

