cards[5]{id,category,difficulty,front,back,source,tags}:
  card_001,research,hard,"What is the primary clinical implication of the AI system described in the ScienceDaily article 'THIS AI SPOTS DANGEROUS BLOOD CELLS DOCTORS OFTEN MISS'?", "Improved diagnostic accuracy for hematological malignancies such as leukemia, potentially leading to earlier and more effective treatment.", "AI;blood cells;diagnosis;leukemia", "ScienceDaily Health"
  card_002,news,medium,"What does the American College of Radiology (ACR) accreditation signify for a healthcare institution like AdventHealth Murray?", "A commitment to high-quality imaging services and adherence to established standards of care, likely enhancing patient trust and referral patterns.", "ACR accreditation;quality assurance;patient care", "Google News Radiology"
  card_003,research,medium,"The article discusses medication safety in dementia care. What is a key concern highlighted?", "Prescribing potentially harmful brain medications to dementia patients without clear medical justification.", "Dementia;medication safety;cognitive impairment", "Google News Radiology"
  card_004,research,medium,"What innovative technology is being developed to improve medication adherence, as described in the MIT study?", "A biodegradable smart pill with a wireless antenna that can confirm medication ingestion.", "Medication adherence;smart pill;ingestion detection", "ScienceDaily Health"
  card_005,research,hard,"According to the ScienceDaily article on childbirth, what novel insights were gained about uterine contractions?", "The intricate interplay of pressure and stretch sensors in the uterus triggers coordinated contractions during labor, potentially offering new avenues for managing stalled labor.", "Childbirth;uterine contractions;physiology;labor management", "ScienceDaily Health"

