  card_003,msk,medium,"According to a long-term study, at what approximate age do physical fitness and strength typically begin to decline?","Around age 35, although later-in-life exercise can still significantly improve physical capacity.","ScienceDaily Health",msk;fitness;aging;strength;exercise
  card_004,abdomen,medium,"Which new primary care approach, focused on patient-requested weight management, showed success in halting population weight gain in a large-scale trial?","PATHWEIGH, a weight management approach, successfully halted population weight gain.","ScienceDaily Health",abdomen;weight management;PATHWEIGH;primary care;public health
