cards[5]{id,category,difficulty,front,back,source,tags}:
  card_001,news,medium,"What is the primary concern highlighted in the news about radiologists?","A significant number of radiologists are leaving a CT hospital, raising concerns about workforce stability and patient care.",courant.com,workforce;radiology;staffing
  card_002,research,medium,"According to recent research, what might be a new understanding of the cause of asthma?","Instead of previously blamed molecules, asthma might be driven by 'pseudo leukotrienes'.",ScienceDaily Health,asthma;research;inflammation
  card_003,research,hard,"What cellular mechanism has been identified that can influence the survival of brain cells?","Sugar metabolism can act as a switch, either promoting neuronal collapse or survival.",ScienceDaily Health,neuroscience;cell survival;metabolism
  card_004,research,medium,"A genetic study suggests a direct link between which three conditions and dementia?","Obesity, high blood pressure, and dementia have a direct genetic link, suggesting a causal relationship.",ScienceDaily Health,dementia;obesity;hypertension
  card_005,research,medium,"What potential long-term metabolic risks are associated with a ketogenic diet, according to a recent study?","A long-term keto diet may trigger metabolic problems like fatty liver disease and impaired blood sugar control.",ScienceDaily Health,keto diet;metabolic risks;liver disease

# Added on 2026-01-30
cards[5]{id,category,difficulty,front,back,source,tags}:
  card_001,news,medium,"What is the primary concern highlighted in the news article regarding radiology practices?", "A major radiology practice is ending its partnership with a hospital three years before their current contract expires, signaling potential financial pressures and shifts in the healthcare landscape.", "Radiology Business",news;healthcare;economics
  card_002,news,medium,"According to the Stanford article, what broader aspects of patient well-being are increasingly being considered within radiology?", "The article suggests a broadening scope for radiologic practice to encompass patient experiences like brain fog and the societal impact of mental health challenges.", "med.stanford.edu",news;patient experience;mental health
  card_003,research,hard,"What is the key mechanism demonstrated in the research on tumor immune cells?", "Researchers have developed a method to reprogram dormant immune cells within tumors to actively destroy cancer cells, representing a significant advancement in immunotherapy.", "ScienceDaily Health",research;immunotherapy;cancer
  card_004,research,medium,"What type of nanoparticles are being developed for potential disease treatment?", "Novel nanoparticles are being developed to target and eliminate disease-causing proteins in tissues, including the brain, offering a potentially less invasive approach to treating cancer and dementia.", "ScienceDaily Health",research;nanoparticles;dementia;cancer
  card_005,research,medium,"What is the potential link identified between fat accumulation and brain health?", "Research using advanced MRI has linked specific patterns of fat accumulation—including pancreatic fat and 'skinny fat'—to accelerated brain aging and increased risk of neurological diseases.", "ScienceDaily Health",research;brain aging;fat;neurology

# Added on 2026-01-31
