cards[5]{id,category,difficulty,front,back,source,tags}:
  card_001,news,medium,"A major radiology practice is ending a hospital partnership 3 years early due to contract disagreements. What is a potential long-term implication of such shifts in hospital-physician relationships?","Increased financial instability for radiology practices and potential changes in how radiology services are delivered.", "Radiology Business", "hospital finance;physician contracts;practice management"
  card_002,research,hard,"Research suggests that weight regain is common after discontinuing popular weight loss drugs like Ozempic. What is a key takeaway regarding long-term weight management?","Long-term weight management requires strategies beyond medication alone.", "ScienceDaily Health", "weight loss;Ozempic;longitudinal studies;patient counseling"
  card_003,research,medium,"Studies indicate that IDH-mutant glioma may originate years before becoming detectable on imaging. What clinical implication does this have for early diagnosis?","The need for further research into early detection biomarkers for this tumor type.", "ScienceDaily Health", "brain tumor;IDH mutation;early detection;biomarkers"
  card_004,research,medium,"A long-term breast cancer vaccine trial showed remarkable survival rates in metastatic disease participants. What does this suggest about the potential of cancer vaccines?","Cancer vaccines can induce durable immune memory and hold promise for future cancer treatments.", "ScienceDaily Health", "cancer vaccine;immunotherapy;metastatic breast cancer;durable response"
  card_005,research,hard,"Researchers at Mount Sinai developed an immunotherapy targeting macrophages to disrupt the tumor's protective environment. What is the proposed mechanism of action of this therapeutic approach?","Disrupting the tumor's protective environment allows the immune system to effectively destroy metastatic cancer cells.", "ScienceDaily Health", "immunotherapy;macrophages;metastasis;tumor microenvironment"

